    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Assistant-Director-of-Recruitment_R-2557": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Recruitment",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-21\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Office of Admissions invites applications for the position of Assistant Director of Recruitment. This position reports to the Director of Admissions and Enrollment Communications and is responsible for leading and managing the team of Admissions Counselors to create goals and objectives related to recruitment initiatives. The Assistant Director of Recruitment collaborates with campus constituents to develop priorities, timelines, and procedures for projects related to the Southeastern Dual Enrollment Program, the Connect to Success Programs with Northshore Technical Community College, and current and developing freshmen success initiatives. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree from an accredited university Experience in higher education PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated experience in Slate, Workday and PeopleSoft student information systems. Experience in higher education student recruiting, admissions, and/or registrar environments. Must maintain an understanding of and assure adherence to NCAA, Southland Conference, and Institutional rules and Louisiana Board of Supervisors regulations. DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES AND SKILLS Must possess the ability to adapt to changing technology and apply technological solutions to business processes, and effectively communicate with a wide variety of higher education constituents including internal and external clients. Must be committed to working with diversity. Must possess a valid Louisiana driver's license and the ability to successfully complete the Southeastern Driver Safety Course. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) Names and contact information for 3 references Posting Close Date October 5, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
