    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Web-Programmer-Developer_R-2581": {
      "title": "Web Programmer/Developer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Office of Technology invites applications for the position of Web Programmer/Developer. The Web Programmer/Developer designs, develops, and maintains dynamic web applications and integrated systems. Primary responsibilities include building secure web interfaces, supporting existing web infrastructure, integrating third-party APIs, and assisting with enterprise systems (CMS, LMS, ERP). The ideal candidate combines technical expertise in full-stack web development with strong collaboration skills to support internal stakeholders and end-users. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree in Computer Science or related field from an accredited university by hire date PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS 2 years of relevant IT experience Experience with PGP/GPG, SSH, and TLS encryption standards Experience designing and coding secure web applicants following industry best practices for maintaining the security and integrity of the application Experience with integrating third party APIs Experience with Accessibility Compliance, including but not limited to WCAG and Section 508 Knowledge of Laravel and Code Igniter frameworks Knowledge of web and database development technologies Knowledge of PHP and MYSQL Knowledge of a version control system such as GIT Knowledge of HTML, JavaScript and CSS Familiarity with network protocols (HTTP, TLS/SSL, LDAP, DNS) and Linux/Unix environments REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Resume/Vita Cover Letter Copies of Transcripts (Official transcripts will be required if hired) Names and contact information for 3 references Posting Close Date September 30, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/HVAC-Refrigeration-Mech_R-2561": {
      "title": "HVAC Refrigeration Mech",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSoutheastern Louisiana University’s Department of Physical Plant Services invites applications for the position of HVAC Refrigeration Mechanic. This position is responsible for a variety of tasks relating to installation, repairs, and maintenance of HVAC systems and refrigeration units across the campus. Duties include diagnosing electrical and mechanical faults and performing tasks such as cleaning, adjusting, and repairing HVAC systems. Hourly Rate: $21.05 EXAMS, LICENSE, AND SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS Applicants must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to be certified through the Southeastern Defensive Driving Course Appropriate EPA refrigerant recycling and recovery certification for technicians (as required under Section 608 of the Clean Air Act, 1990). Southeastern requires a Type IV, Universal Certification. Please note that Southeastern will allow the candidate selected for the job up to 30 days to acquire the required certification. Additional information regarding technician certification requirements and programs may be obtained by calling the Stratospheric Ozone Protection Hotline at (800) 296-1996 (10am-4pm Eastern Time, Monday-Friday except federal holidays) or by visiting the EPA's Stratospheric Ozone Depletion Web Site at www.epa.gov/ozone/title6/608. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Two years of experience or training in the installation and/or maintenance of heating, ventilating, or air conditioning systems. When applying, you should list all Education and Work Experience on this application. When listing your Work Experience, indicate if the job was full-time or part-time and what percentage of time you spent on each of the duties listed. This information will be used to determine if you meet the Minimum Qualifications of the position. If complete information is not listed, it may result in your application not being considered. *Resumes WILL NOT be accepted in lieu of completed education and experience sections on your application. There is no guarantee that everyone who applies to this posting will be interviewed. The hiring supervisor/manager has 90 days from the closing date of the posting to make a hiring decision. Click Here to View the Civil Service Job Spec Posting Close Date September 28, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. HR Contact If you have questions about this position, the application process or need special accommodations, please call the Human Resources Office at (985) 549-2001 or send an email to jobs@southeastern.edu."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Financial-Reporting-Accountant_R-2568": {
      "title": "Financial Reporting Accountant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Department of the Controller's Office invites applications for the position of Financial Reporting Accountant. The major function of this position is financial accounting duties, including bank reconciliations, asset management, sales tax preparation and reconciliation, and journals. This position will also assist in the preparation of the annual financial report, annual athletic reports, and any other reports requested by the system office and OSRAP with all applicable federal and state requirements. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS 5 years of accounting or auditing experience Bachelor's degree in Accounting Other Bachelor's degree may be substituted for Bachelor's degree in Accounting with at least seven years of accounting or auditing experience. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master's Degree DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES AND SKILLS Define problems, establish facts, collect data, and draw valid conclusions Familiarity with and ability to operate office equipment including typewriters, calculators, and personal computers, with or without a reasonable accommodation Basic mathematical skills (addition, subtraction, multiplication and division) REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) Names and contact information for 3 references Posting Close Date September 29, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Financial-Aid-Counselor_R-2572": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Office of Financial Aid invites applications for the position of Financial Aid Counselor. This position reports to the Assistant Director of Financial Aid. The Financial Aid Counselor's duties include counseling and advising students and parents on the various financial aid programs, assisting with the administration of one or more federal, state, or institutional financial aid programs, evaluating Financial Aid applications in order to determine student eligibility for various financial aid programs, and collecting data and keeping accurate records. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree from an accredited university by hire date PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience in financial aid administration, or related experience Experience in a highly automated, financial aid office at an institution which resembles Southeastern Louisiana University in size and complexity of program administration DESIRED KNOWLEDGE, ABILITIES AND SKILLS Proficient with automated data management Strong organizational skills Strong communication, customer service and public relation skills Knowledge or skill in various software applications including Microsoft Word and data management tools REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume Copies of Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) Names and contact information for 3 references Posting Close Date September 28, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Educational-Technology-Administrator_R-2573": {
      "title": "Educational Technology Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Office of Technology invites applications for the position of Educational Technology Administrator. The Office of Technology is committed to supporting the core business processes of the university, particularly supporting online education. The Educational Technology Administrator serves as the primary administrator for Southeastern's Learning Management System (Canvas). In addition, the Educational Technology Administrator serves as the contact for elevated support cases. The Educational Technology Administrator is responsible for overseeing the development and implementation of strategic initiatives to integrate technology effectively into academic programs, including the administration of the learning management system. The Administrator works closely with the Center for Faculty Excellence to support faculty and administrators in leveraging technology to achieve educational goals. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree from an accredited university by hire date Minimum of 2 years of experience with technology/systems administration Experience working with educational technologies, various forms of new media, and relevant subject-specific technology Knowledge of Artificial Intelligence (AI) tools and their integration within higher education environments PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with diverse stakeholders Familiarity with higher education systems, including Student Information Systems (SIS), third-party LTI integrations, and accessibility compliance tools Familiarity with higher education processes, such as term start and end-of-term workflows, academic checkpoint monitoring, and section cross-listing/merging Track record of implementing successful educational technology initiatives Ability to adapt to rapidly evolving technology and educational trends Fiscally responsible with technology solutions Experience developing and delivering professional development programs for faculty Commitment to working with a diverse group of faculty, student workers and graduate assistants REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Copies of Transcripts (Official transcripts required upon hire) Names and contact information for three (3) professional references Posting Close Date September 28, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Guard_R-2577": {
      "title": "Guard",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSoutheastern Louisiana University Department of Transportation Services invites applications for the position of Guard. Join our team in providing a safe, secure, and welcoming environment for students, employees, and visitors. This position performs security patrols of campus buildings and grounds, monitors access to facilities, responds to emergencies and disturbances, and helps maintain public safety. Responsibilities also include directing traffic, enforcing parking regulations, issuing citations, coordinating vehicle impoundments, installing traffic control devices, maintaining departmental equipment, and providing excellent customer service. The successful candidate will communicate effectively with the public, assist during athletic and special events, complete accurate documentation, and work collaboratively to support daily campus operations while ensuring compliance with university policies and regulations. Current salary: $12.84/hour When applying, you should list all Education and Work Experience on this application. When listing your Work Experience, indicate if the job was full-time or part-time and what percentage of time you spent on each of the duties listed. This information will be used to determine if you meet the Minimum Qualifications of the position. If complete information is not listed, it may result in your application not being considered. *Resumes WILL NOT be accepted in lieu of completed education and experience sections on your application. Applicants must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to be certified through the Southeastern Defensive Driving Course. No Civil Service test score is required in order to be considered for this vacancy. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS No experience or training is required. NECESSARY SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS: An applicant who has been convicted of a felony or who is under indictment on a felony charge will be disqualified until relief from the disabilities imposed by state and federal laws is granted. Applicants must be at least 18 years of age. Applicants may be required to possess a current Louisiana driver's license. Click Here to View the Civil Service Job Spec Posting Close Date September 28, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application, which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. HR Contact If you have questions about this position, the application process or need special accommodations, please call the Human Resources Office at (985) 549-2001 or send an email to jobs@southeastern.edu."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Academic-Advisor_R-2562": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University’s College of Honors and Excellence's Office for First Year Success invites applications for the position of College Success Advisor. The College Success Advisor (CSA) supports the transition of sophomores into the College and provides proactive advising and early intervention for students from sophomores through seniors on academic probation in the College of Arts, Humanities & Social Sciences (AHSS). Embedded within AHSS and reporting to the director of First-Year Success, this position works in close partnership with faculty advisors, the First-Year Success office, the Academic & Career Exploration office, and the Tinsley Learning Center to support students through the critical transition from the first to second year and to serve as a resource for holistic student success support for at-risk students. QUALIFICATIONS Required: Master's degree from an accredited university conferred by hire date. Experience in academic advising, student success, or a related student-facing role Strong interpersonal and communication skills; ability to work across academic departments Preferred: Degree in counseling or an AHSS major Familiarity with early alert systems and data-informed advising practice Experience advising at-risk or first-generation student populations Knowledge of financial aid processes and student support resources NACADA membership or participation in professional advising organizations REQUIRED DOCUMENTS: Cover Letter Resume/Vita Copies of Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired) Names and contact information for 3 references Posting Close Date September 30, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    },
    "https://ulsselu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/SLU/job/Hammond-La/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor_R-2547": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThank you for your interest in employment with Southeastern Louisiana University. Southeastern Louisiana University's Department of Accounting and Finance in the College of Business seeks to fill an Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting position. This position involves teaching undergraduate graduate-level courses in accounting, conducting research, and participating in service to the department, college, and university. All areas of accounting will be considered. The start date for the position is August 2027. Candidates must possess a commitment to teaching and conducting quality research. Candidates must be committed to working with diversity. Both the college and the accounting program are AACSB accredited. The accounting program first achieved supplemental accreditation in 1993. The faculty values collegiality and works well together in a student-focused environment. The program graduates approximately 90 students with a B.S. in Accounting annually. Southeastern Louisiana University is a progressive regional, comprehensive university that enrolls approximately 15,000 graduate and undergraduate students. The University is accredited by Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges (SACSCOC). The University’s home, Hammond, LA, is at the crossroads of Interstates 55 and 12 and a part of Louisiana’s thriving Northshore of Lake Pontchartrain, the fastest growing region in the state. It is centrally located within an hour’s drive of New Orleans, Baton Rouge (the state capitol), and the Mississippi Gulf Coast. Hammond affords extensive cultural, recreational, and research opportunities. REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS:  A terminal degree in accounting from an AACSB accredited program is required. ABD status will be considered. Teaching experience and professional certification in accounting are desired. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS Cover Letter Resume/CV Transcripts for terminal degree (all official transcripts would be required upon employment) Posting Close Date September 28, 2026 Please Note:  Applications must be completed and submitted by 11:59 p.m. on the posting close date to ensure consideration. Southeastern Louisiana University is committed to fostering an environment of inclusion, respect and appreciation of differences in individuals. Southeastern is also designated as a State as a Model Employer (SAME) agency and provides assistance to persons needing accommodations or with the accessibility of materials. How to Apply: Click on the Apply button and complete an electronic application which can be used for this vacancy as well as future vacancies. Any required documents should be attached under the Resume/CV section of your application. If all required documents are not attached you will NOT be considered ."
    }
